# Install-script allowlist
#
# One entry per dependency that is permitted to run an install lifecycle
# script. A dependency that runs no install script still needs an entry when
# it is newly added, so the decision is recorded rather than assumed.
#
# Format: <package-name>  # reason
#
# Verified 2026-11-08 against the installed package manifests: each package
# below declares no install, postinstall, prepare, or prepublish script.

commander  # CLI argument parser; pure JS, no build step, no install script
vitest  # test runner; ships prebuilt binaries per platform, no install script
typescript  # compiler; ships prebuilt binaries per platform, no install script
@types/node  # type declarations only; no runtime code, no install script
